---
layout: base.njk
comments: true
eleventyComputed:
  # A photo may carry its own one-line `description:` in front matter. Where it
  # does, that is the meta description and the search-result snippet; where it
  # does not, fall back to the generated formula. The fallback is deliberately
  # kept - a photo with nothing worth saying about it should not be forced to
  # invent something, and the formula is better than an empty tag.
  description: "{{ description if description else title + ' — ' + category + ' photograph, ' + location + ', ' + year + '.' }}"
---
<article class="photo-detail">
  {# A panel picture (`panels:` in front matter) is also cut into one slice per
     panel from the same JPEG, stacked; the CSS shows the strip on a wide
     screen and the stack on a narrow one, never both. The hidden one is
     display:none, so a screen reader meets the alt text once. Geometry and
     rationale: lib/panels.js. #}
  <img class="photo-detail__image{% if panels %} photo-detail__image--strip{% endif %}" src="/images/photos/{{ image }}" alt="{{ alt }}" />
  {% if panels %}
  <div class="photo-detail__panels" role="img" aria-label="{{ alt }}">
    {% for s in image | panelSlices(panels) %}
    <div class="photo-detail__panel" style="aspect-ratio: {{ s.aspect }}"><img src="/images/photos/{{ image }}" alt="" style="width: {{ s.width }}%; margin-left: {{ s.left }}%; margin-top: {{ s.top }}%" /></div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
  {% endif %}
  <h1 class="page-title">{{ title }}</h1>

  {# Optional note. Renders only when the .md file has body text, so photos
     without one look finished rather than incomplete. The house rule for
     writing one: never describe what is visible - add what is not. #}
  {% if content %}
  <div class="photo-note">{{ content | safe }}</div>
  {% endif %}
  {# Two groups of rows: what the picture is (category, subjects, the two
     derived scopes), then where and when it was taken. Subjects overlap, so
     it is the one row that can hold several links; the wild-or-cultivated
     facet was labelled "Subject" until 3 September 2026 and is now named for
     what it is - a scope laid over the subjects, not the subject itself. #}
  {# Every row below links to an archive page built from listed photos only.
     An unlisted page can be the sole holder of its album, location, year or
     subject, in which case that archive does not exist; hasGroup (in
     .eleventy.js) checks, and the row falls back to plain text rather than a
     link to a page that was never built. #}
  <dl class="photo-meta">
    {# A competition result, when there is one. First in the list because it
       is the one row a visitor did not come expecting, and a fact rather
       than a judgement: the placing, then the competition, one string. #}
    {% if award %}
    <div class="photo-meta__row">
      <dt>Award</dt>
      <dd>{{ award }}</dd>
    </div>
    {% endif %}
    <div class="photo-meta__row">
      <dt>Category</dt>
      <dd>{% if collections.photoCategorys | hasGroup(category) %}<a href="/category/{{ category | slugify }}/">{{ category }}</a>{% else %}{{ category }}{% endif %}</dd>
    </div>
    {% if subjects and subjects.length %}
    <div class="photo-meta__row">
      <dt>Subjects</dt>
      <dd>{% for s in subjects %}{% if collections.photoSubjects | hasGroup(s) %}<a href="/subjects/{{ s | slugify }}/">{{ s }}</a>{% else %}{{ s }}{% endif %}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}</dd>
    </div>
    {% endif %}
    {% set grown = { category: category, competitions: competitions, wild_or_cultivated: wild_or_cultivated } | wildOrCultivated %}
    {% if grown %}
    <div class="photo-meta__row">
      <dt>Wild or cultivated</dt>
      <dd>{% if collections.photoWildOrCultivated | hasGroup(grown) %}<a href="/wild-or-cultivated/{{ grown | slugify }}/">{{ grown }}</a>{% else %}{{ grown }}{% endif %}</dd>
    </div>
    {% endif %}
    {% set place = { category: category, competitions: competitions, setting: setting } | naturalOrBuilt %}
    {% if place %}
    <div class="photo-meta__row">
      <dt>Setting</dt>
      <dd>{% if collections.photoNaturalOrBuilt | hasGroup(place) %}<a href="/natural-or-built/{{ place | slugify }}/">{{ place }}</a>{% else %}{{ place }}{% endif %}</dd>
    </div>
    {% endif %}
    <div class="photo-meta__row">
      <dt>Location</dt>
      <dd>{% if collections.photoLocations | hasGroup(location) %}<a href="/location/{{ location | slugify }}/">{{ location }}</a>{% else %}{{ location }}{% endif %}</dd>
    </div>
    {% set country = location | countryOf %}
    {% if country %}
    <div class="photo-meta__row">
      <dt>Country</dt>
      <dd>{% if collections.photoCountries | hasGroup(country) %}<a href="/country/{{ country | slugify }}/">{{ country }}</a>{% else %}{{ country }}{% endif %}</dd>
    </div>
    {% endif %}
    <div class="photo-meta__row">
      <dt>Year</dt>
      <dd>{% if collections.photoYears | hasGroup(year) %}<a href="/year/{{ year }}/">{{ year }}</a>{% else %}{{ year }}{% endif %}</dd>
    </div>
    {% if album %}
    <div class="photo-meta__row">
      <dt>Album</dt>
      <dd>{% if collections.photoAlbums | hasGroup(album) %}<a href="/albums/{{ album | slugify }}/">{{ album }}</a>{% else %}{{ album }}{% endif %}</dd>
    </div>
    {% endif %}
  </dl>
  <p class="photo-license">
    © {{ copyrightYear }} Dermot R. Cochran — licensed under
    <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/">CC BY-NC-ND 4.0</a>.
  </p>
  <p><a href="/gallery/">← Back to Gallery</a></p>
</article>
